// handleSearchEmailsRequest handles searchEmails operation.
//
// Searches inbound emails with structured filters and optional
// full-text matching across parsed email fields. This endpoint is
// optimized for filtered inbox views and CLI polling workflows:
// callers that only need new accepted mail can pass
// `sort=received_at_asc`, `snippet=false`, `include_facets=false`,
// and a `date_from` timestamp.
// `q`, `subject`, and `body` use the same English full-text index
// as the web inbox search. Structured filters such as `from`, `to`,
// `domain_id`, status, attachment presence, and spam score bounds
// are combined with the text query.
// The text parameters (`q`, `from`, `to`, `subject` and `body`) must not
// contain a NUL character; a value that does is rejected with a 400
// validation error.
// Connected-agent credentials search only mail received by their own
// address. This applies to results, totals, facets, and every page;
// search filters cannot widen the credential's scope. When
// `reply_to_sent_email_id` is supplied, its parent send must belong
// to the connected address in the same organization. An unavailable
// parent returns 404. Sender filters are not authentication proof;
// inspect the email detail's authentication evidence before trusting it.
// Agent connection keys (pconn_) may search only mail received by their bound address. This
// restriction applies to results, totals, facets and pagination; from/to and q filters cannot widen
// it. When reply_to_sent_email_id is supplied, the parent must be a send from the connected address
// in the same organization, otherwise the response is 404. The parent filter is optional. Existing
// from/to filters are substring or domain filters, not proof of sender identity. Inspect getEmail
// authentication details before trusting a sender.
